  "summary": "When Tim Costello was in year 9 (around 15 years old), he asked his teacher if poverty happens naturally, like the sun rising or tides moving. His teacher said no — poverty is caused by human decisions and policies, not nature. This idea stayed with him and shaped his life. Now 69 years old, Costello has spent more than 30 years working to fight poverty in Australia and around the world, including in war zones and disaster areas. He has also been a mayor, written books, and is well known as a Baptist minister and former CEO of World Vision, a major aid organization. He's so famous that some people mix him up with his brother, Peter Costello, who was a politician. In fact, people often ask if he’s the 'political brother' or the 'religious one'. Tim is the religious one, known for his charity and social justice work."
}
